      "writtenOn": "2023-10-09T22:44:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem in b/290914667 is that candidates for the secondary are cached prior to the pairing with primary. Only after pairing can we find out that this candidate is actually the same as the primary.\n\nThis fix is trying to rule out the candidate during the initial device discovery phase. However at this point, we may haven\u0027t paired with the primary, so BTM may not be able to resolve the candidate RPA.",
      "revId": "eb1a50883ef7ff1acc657cc7635d554ef968a583",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e1a60a2_e61e5eac",
        "filename": "system/bta/csis/csis_client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1320,
      "author": {
        "id": 1087037
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-10T07:26:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You found one bud, either primary or secondary.\nAfter you bonded it, and connected CSIP profile you start scan.\n\nSo when you reach this code, you are for sure bonded to one bud, and the 2nd one is not bonded.\n\nso here, we check if the result matches (either by identity address or RPA) to already bonded bud, and if it\u0027s the case we want to skip it.\n\nif device is just cached, it won\u0027t have a link key known.",
      "parentUuid": "6e2dc2ef_b45fe109",
      "revId": "eb1a50883ef7ff1acc657cc7635d554ef968a583",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
